    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d825">

                <pb facs="1107" n="1001" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg1001"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-28T03:00:00+03:00">October 28, 1939—3
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 28—1:38 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>822. I have learned that the German Embassy has received information from
                    Murmansk that the German prize crew was put back on board the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> yesterday. I further understand that
                    members of that Embassy are expressing their conviction that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> will be successfully brought to a
                    German port by remaining within Scandinavian territorial waters on the voyage
                    from Murmansk to Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
